I was wearing a cursed ring of polymorph (don't ask, please) and polymorphed
into a scorpion or something while in a shop.  As my armor and weapons
crashed to the floor, they were sold to the shopkeeper without asking if I
actually wanted to sell them or not.  However, even as a scorpion I could
drop a potion and get asked by the shopkeeper if I want to sell.  It seems
to me that if you turn into a "non-sentient" being while in a shop and 
drop a bunch of stuff (either intentionally or unintentionally), either the 
shopkeeper should keep it and not give you any money (since you're just a 
bloody scorpion) or you should be asked whether you want to sell it.  I guess 
this is probably related to eating a tin of fried whatnot in a shop, too.   
Also, if a dog carries something into a shop and drops it, the shopkeeper
just keeps it (unless Fido and the shopkeeper have something going on 
behind my back...it bears thinking about), so there is a precedent for not
paying peaceful "animals".  

Just seemed a little inconsistent.  

